      "## What prompted the proceedings",
      "The petitioners alleged that gifts, hospitality, travel sponsorship and other inducements could influence prescribing. The Court considered existing oversight and material presented by the parties and intervenors. It identified concerns about the effectiveness of the existing framework while recognising that the detailed design of regulation calls for consultation and executive consideration. (Paras. 1–22.)",
