      "## Why the employees wanted the older rules",
      "The employees were officiating in the post formerly called Assistant Director (Official Language). They argued that vacancies and rights under the earlier rules entitled them to consideration without the qualifying test prescribed under the 2005 rules. The High Court agreed and directed consideration on that footing.",
      "## Why the date of vacancy was insufficient",
      "Applying the principle in *Raj Kumar*, the Supreme Court explained that creation of a vacancy does not by itself give an employee a vested right to have it filled under the rules then in force. The applicable rules at consideration and any lawful policy decision about filling vacancies matter. It reversed the High Court and allowed the appeals. (Paras. 12–14 and preceding reasoning.)",
