      "The Court held that equal pay for equal work calls for comparison across relevant factors. It found the prior teaching experience of the transferred or promoted group provided a rational basis for the difference in this scheme. It dismissed the appeals and disposed of pending applications. Its reasoning leaves room for a parity claim where the relevant factors truly are equivalent. (Judgment, analysis and paras. 18–20.)",
