    "lead": "The Supreme Court gave effect to a voluntary settlement and dissolved the marriage under Article 142. The proceedings began as a request to transfer a case between family courts.",
    "body": [
      "[Read the judgment and download the SCR PDF](https://thelegalchronicles.com/judgments/supreme-court/2026/sakshi-sharma-versus-aman-sinha-4a62d723)",
      "## How the parties reached agreement",
      "Divorce and maintenance proceedings were pending in Rajasthan. The husband filed a separate proceeding for restitution of conjugal rights in Delhi. The wife requested transfer to Alwar, and the Supreme Court referred their dispute to its mediation centre. The settlement led to a joint application asking the Court to give effect to the terms.",
      "## Why the Court granted complete relief",
      "The Court spoke with the parties and recorded that the agreement was voluntary, the disputes had been resolved and reconciliation was not possible. The husband handed over a ₹20 lakh demand draft in court and the Court recorded compliance with the remaining terms. It allowed the joint application, disposed of the transfer petition, directed communication to the courts and authorities concerned and ordered preparation of the divorce decree. The relief arose from this settlement and the Supreme Court’s Article 142 power. (Paras. 8–18.)",
      "*AI-assisted editorial explanation. Independent human legal review has not been performed.*"
    ],
