    "title": "Why delay charges were excluded from insolvency costs in a stalled housing project",
    "metadata": [
      "**Case** The Authorised Representative for Granite Gate Properties Private Limited, Ms. Rakesh Verma v. M/s New Okhla Industrial Development Authority and Ors. · 2026 INSC 952 · [2026] 9 S.C.R. 434",
      "**Decided** 03 September 2026 · (Civil Appeal No. 3132 of 2026)",
      "**Bench as recorded by SCR** [J.B. Pardiwala and K. Vinod Chandran,* JJ.]"
    ],
    "lead": "The Supreme Court set aside the direction treating NOIDA’s lease extension charges as costs of the corporate insolvency resolution process in this particular project. It allowed the homebuyers’ representative’s appeal and dismissed NOIDA’s appeal for charges over a longer period.",
    "body": [
      "[Read the judgment and download the SCR PDF](https://thelegalchronicles.com/judgments/supreme-court/2026/the-authorised-representative-for-granite-gate-properties-private-limite-13f6f1e8)",
      "## Why the costs mattered",
      "The developer became a corporate debtor while homebuyers were still waiting for their homes. The homebuyers pooled funds to keep the project going during insolvency and were the creditors who approved the resolution plan. The NCLAT treated time extension charges on two leases as insolvency costs up to the maximum three years contemplated in the leases. The representative challenged inclusion, while NOIDA sought a longer period.",
      "## Why the Court removed the charge from that category",
      "The Court considered the purpose of the housing development, the prolonged delay and the burden of passing the charge to the resolution applicant and homebuyers. It held that the penalty could not validly be imposed that way in the circumstances and removed the direction to treat the charges as insolvency costs. It framed the result in the peculiar facts of this project. (Judgment, analysis and paras. 16–18.)",
      "*AI-assisted editorial explanation. Independent human legal review has not been performed.*"
    ],
