    "metadata": [
      "**Case** Shirish Pandharinath Patil v. The State of Maharashtra & Ors. · 2026 INSC 949 · [2026] 9 S.C.R. 428",
      "**Decided** 03 September 2026 · (Civil Appeal No. 12169 of 2026)",
      "**Bench as recorded by SCR** [Aravind Kumar and Vipul M. Pancholi,* JJ.]"
    ],
    "lead": "The Supreme Court protected Shirish Patil’s retirement and pension benefits under Article 142 while leaving the invalidation of his Scheduled Tribe claim in place.",
    "body": [
      "[Read the judgment and download the SCR PDF](https://thelegalchronicles.com/judgments/supreme-court/2026/shirish-pandharinath-patil-versus-the-state-of-maharashtra-ors-cc3151c5)",
      "## What the appeal sought",
      "A scrutiny committee invalidated the claim to Tokre Koli Scheduled Tribe status and the High Court upheld that decision. Patil sought protection of retirement benefits in the alternative. He had served since 1994 and retired in June 2025 after continuing in employment under an interim Supreme Court order.",
      "## Why the protection was limited",
      "The Court acknowledged that invalidation normally has legal consequences. It considered the length of service, retirement and the statement on record that no family member had derived a benefit under the certificate. It partially allowed the appeal to protect retirement benefits as an exceptional measure. The certificate was not restored, and it cannot support a future benefit for him or a family member. (Judgment, analysis and paras. 15–17.)",
      "*AI-assisted editorial explanation. Independent human legal review has not been performed.*"
    ],
