      "## How the trials became linked",
      "The accused sought to pause a sessions trial because the same persons faced proceedings under the Uttar Pradesh Gangsters and Anti-Social Activities (Prevention) Act. The trial court refused. The High Court directed that the ordinary trial be put on hold and the Gangsters Act case expedited.",
      "## Why precedence did not compel a standstill",
      "The Court interpreted the statutory precedence rule in light of Article 21 and the purpose of both proceedings. An automatic halt could delay other cases in a way inconsistent with the right to speedy trial. It reversed the High Court and recorded that the ordinary trial had already concluded under an interim Supreme Court order. Its decision addresses the stay of proceedings. (Judgment, analysis and paras. 26–28.)",
